kunzite: Adreno 710, glue plan K3 (main repo ios/gpu-glue-plan.md 3.2, 4): submission.
redwood_gpu_submit/_done/_last/_report are real. Once the CP runs out of secure mode (step 24, or
keep mode before it says ready), a fence word at scratch + 0x200 is read through an uncached alias
of the scratch page (unmapped by the undo), and a submission takes the IBs as kgsl's gen7 ringbuffer
does (gen7_ringbuffer_addcmds and _submitcmd): CP_THREAD_CONTROL both, CP_SET_MARKER 0x101 (IFPC
off), BR; the IB list between markers 0xd and 0xe, one CP_INDIRECT_BUFFER_PFE each; CCU invalidate
events 24 and 25; the fence, CP_EVENT_WRITE CACHE_CLEAN | BIT(27) writing the submission's number
once the work is done (no BIT(31): we poll); both threads, marker 0x100 (IFPC on), BR: 25 + 4 per IB
words, under a mutex. The ring wraps: a short tail is covered by a CP_NOP and the words go from 0
(adreno_ringbuffer_allocspace), and the submitter waits up to 2 s for RPTR to make room; WPTR never
catches up with it. _done compares the fence word, _last is the newest number, _report prints fence,
ring, RBBM, CP fault, interrupt and protect status, SQE stat, IB1/IB2 base and remaining size, and
context 0's FSR/FAR/FSYNR0. redwood_gpu_ready() now also wants the submission set up; the keep
report shows the fence; the keep mode's exit waits for the last fence before the undo. Step 19 maps
the scratch page unprivileged too (the fence is written by the CP's event path, not certainly a
privileged master: boot #43's fault was such a write). Step 23 cleans its marker's line out of the
CPU cache before reading it (boot #49 read a stale one). Step 24 (kgpu=24; with kgpu_keep: 1-21, 23,
24, kept): IBs in an own buffer of the GPU's, a 1024x256 picture: one IB of three bands; two IBs in
one submission; 400 submissions of a one-row IB without waiting, around the ring; every fence the
one after the last, done(last) and not done(last + 1); the samples checked after the fences alone
(no wait-for-idle or marker in the IBs); the report. Test: kgpu=24 kgpu_keep=1 kgpu_keep_s=120: "THE
GPU RUNS SUBMISSIONS", then kept and undone as on #49.

